{"id": "EUVD-2026-70342", "enisaUuid": "32540511-7eda-3104-a6bc-a74180712db6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Check sk_state before sk_protocol in bpf_tcp_*_syncookie\n\nbpf_tcp_gen_syncookie and bpf_tcp_check_syncookie accept a socket pointer\n'sk' with argument type ARG_PTR_TO_BTF_ID_SOCK_COMMON. However, they access\nsk->sk_protocol without validating whether 'sk' represents a full socket.\n\nFix this issue by checking sk->sk_state != TCP_LISTEN before inspecting\nsk->sk_protocol in both bpf_tcp_gen_syncookie and bpf_tcp_check_syncookie.\nSince mini-sockets are never in the TCP_LISTEN state, the condition\nshort-circuits and prevents dereferencing fullsock-specific fields.", "datePublished": "2026-09-03T08:21:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:47:01", "baseScore": 7.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:L", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5702e4c259809c760912c477c4ae34e9217bb4d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5525e853a2a08a9559adb84b0616025958dc542", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22c2169770ad3b3595690e51caac875178cf496d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23f682083aa3fbc0c49667818efd6979a8bc5ac2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/31a420a822ff92e2090bd5d65efe8e34e2d6d9b8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-83j6-pc2m-jhg5", "CVE-2026-80738"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0db38e86-7eb3-358f-9eba-6aea09266b58", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "399040847084a69f345e0a52fd62f04654e0fce3 <b5525e853a2a08a9559adb84b0616025958dc542"}, {"id": "0e19d8e7-7901-3e67-9b6e-9ca995b7e86e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "399040847084a69f345e0a52fd62f04654e0fce3 <5702e4c259809c760912c477c4ae34e9217bb4d9"}, {"id": "1cdafbcf-97ce-342d-8884-91cfc7b30627", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "39904084